# Woodpecker campaign working files.
#
# Each of these is created by one step and consumed by a later step of the SAME
# workflow. While they were neither tracked nor ignored, the evidence guard in
# the later step saw them as a dirty tree and refused -- a workflow failing on
# files it had just created itself, reported as though the checkout were dirty.
# The receipts are per-run CI outputs, and the two fixture inputs are built
# from unifi-emu at a pinned commit for a scratch image, so none of them
# belong in the tree.
build/**/*-ci.json
/m3-candidate/
/.woodpecker/fixtures/catalog-acceptance/unifi-emu
/.woodpecker/fixtures/catalog-acceptance/devices.fleet.json
/upgrade-plan-runner
